# Domain Vocabulary

Use the names in `docs/API_CONTRACT.md` and `docs/DATABASE_DESIGN.md`. Do not invent synonyms.

| Term | Use this name |
|---|---|
| Role codes | `SALES_REP`, `SALES_MANAGER` |
| Signal types | `procurement`, `technology_initiative`, `leadership_change`, `funding_budget`, `strategic_announcement`, `competitor_vendor`, `contract_renewal` |
| Signal state | `detected`, `validated`, `rejected`, `merged`, `superseded` |
| Score bands | `high`, `medium`, `low`, `monitor` |
| Content layer | `fact`, `interpretation`, `potential_opportunity`, `recommended_action` |
| Cached data | `data_origin` `cached` |

The seven signal types are closed. Both roles see every tracked organization. There is no assignment filter.

Say "potential opportunity" and "may indicate". Do not say a procurement event is guaranteed.
